    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Greystones is pleased to bring No. 24 Druids Court to the market, a generously proportioned two-bedroom apartment enjoying an enviable ground floor position within the renowned Druids Glen Hotel & Golf Resort. Set in this exceptional resort environment, the property combines well-appointed accommodation with a peaceful woodland setting and all the advantages of life within one of Wicklow's most sought-after residential and leisure destinations.\nExtending across approximately 360 acres of beautifully landscaped grounds, Druids Glen provides an outstanding backdrop to everyday life. Residents enjoy beautifully maintained communal areas, designated parking and ample visitor spaces, together with electric vehicle charging facilities. The resort is also home to a luxury hotel and excellent leisure amenities, including a gym and swimming pool, while golf enthusiasts are particularly well catered for with both Druids Heath and the championship Druids Glen course close at hand. The combination of extensive grounds, leisure facilities and tranquil surroundings creates a wonderfully relaxed setting, while the apartment remains conveniently positioned for Greystones, Kilcoole and Newtownmountkennedy.\nNo. 24 occupies a ground floor position and enjoys an appealing south-westerly orientation, extending from the entrance hall through to the kitchen and private patio. This orientation brings a lovely quality of natural light to the apartment, while the patio itself enjoys a sheltered and pleasantly private position. With its sunny aspect, it provides a wonderful outdoor setting for morning coffee, relaxed entertaining or dining al fresco while enjoying the peaceful surroundings.\nOn entering, the quality of the apartment is immediately apparent. The welcoming hallway is finished with beautiful solid timber flooring, which continues through the main accommodation and gives the interiors a warm, cohesive and sophisticated feel. The generous proportions throughout are complemented by a tasteful finish, creating an inviting home that is both comfortable and easy to maintain.\nThe kitchen is well appointed and practical, featuring tiled flooring, a good selection of fitted cabinetry and a range of integrated appliances. Sliding patio doors provide direct access to the private south-facing patio, creating a natural connection between the interior and outdoor space. A useful storage room is conveniently accessed from the patio.\nBeyond the kitchen, double glass doors open into the exceptionally generous living/dining room. This is a particularly impressive space, with proportions that would be equally at home within a much larger family residence. A feature gas fireplace provides a focal point and adds warmth and character to the room, while a large window draws the surrounding woodland into the view and gives the reception space a wonderfully peaceful atmosphere. A glass-panelled door leads directly from the room out to the communal gardens, with the surrounding woodland beyond, creating a lovely connection between the interior and the tranquil natural setting.\n\nThe two bedrooms are both well-proportioned doubles and benefit from fitted wardrobes. Bedroom 1 enjoys the attractive woodland outlook and further benefits from its own en-suite shower room, while Bedroom 2 has a lovely southerly aspect overlooking the landscaped communal grounds to the front of the apartment. A separate bathroom completes the accommodation.\nOne of the great attractions of No. 24 is the combination of generous internal accommodation and an appealing outdoor space, all within the unique surroundings of Druids Glen. The apartment would make an excellent permanent home for those seeking a low-maintenance lifestyle, while its own-door access, ground floor position and private patio also make it particularly well suited as a lock-up-and-leave property. It should equally appeal to investors seeking a property in an established and highly regarded resort setting.\nEarly viewing is strongly recommended to appreciate the generous proportions, attractive presentation and superb surroundings that combine to make No. 24 Druids Court such an appealing home.\nFeatures of Note:\n• Spacious 2-bedroom ground floor apartment\n• Accommodation extending to approximately 90 sq. m.\n• Own-door access\n• Sheltered private south-facing patio\n• Attractive south-westerly orientation\n• Generous living/dining room\n• Feature gas fireplace in living room\n• Pleasant woodland outlook from the living room\n• Two generous double bedrooms with fitted wardrobes\n• En-suite shower room to Bedroom 1\n• Solid timber flooring throughout the main accommodation\n• Tiled kitchen floor\n• Integrated kitchen appliances\n• Gas-fired central heating\n• Double-glazed windows\n• Designated parking space\n• Ample visitor parking\n• Electric vehicle charging points available\n• External storage room\n• Beautifully maintained communal gardens\n• Set within approximately 360 acres at Druids Glen Hotel & Golf Resort\n• Walking distance to Druids Heath Golf Course\n• Adjacent to Druids Glen Championship Golf Course\n• Approximately 7.4 km to Greystones, including DART, seafront and Main Street\n• Approximately 3.3 km to Newtownmountkennedy\n• Approximately 2.6 km to Kilcoole\nManaging Agent: Byrne & Moore\nAnnual Service Charge: 2414 (including sinking fund)"
      },
